If OpenCode ever gets stuck or gives you an error about Playwright not finding the HTML file, use its built-in plan agent.

Before running a big code generation step, you can type @plan in the OpenCode terminal and ask: "Review the pathing logic between my Python worker and the HTML template folder. Are there any absolute vs. relative path issues?" This lets the AI analyze your codebase safely without breaking what it already built.

